  <static seed="1919" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/AbsoluteValue11.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ |{6}|= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ |{-6}|= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ -|{6}|= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ -|{-6}|= }</m> <fillin characters="6" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>The absolute value of <m>6</m> measures how many units are between <m>6</m> and <m>0</m> on the number line, so <m>|{6}|=6</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The absolute value of <m>-6</m> measures how many units are between <m>-6</m> and <m>0</m> on the number line, so <m>|{-6}|=6</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The absolute value symbols cannot affect what are outside them, so we have <m>-|{6}|=-6</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Similar to Part c, we have <m>-|{-6}|=-6</m>.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
